      "writtenOn": "2017-07-10T22:48:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was pretty surprised to see IpSecService return an \"OK\" status with an invalid SPI. It looks like IpSecManager checks for this possibility, but as I look close at netd, I don\u0027t think this is a scenario that needs a test.\n\nIn particular, the INetd interface should never return a 0 value, but should return a binder error/exception instead. We can assume that our mock netd interface behaves correctly according to its interface, and then add netd (XfrmController) tests which ensure it also behaves correctly. (I will grant that the INetd.aidl comments are a bit misleading on this topic.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 125,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 37
